  "title": "Modes of Payment in the Philippines (2026 Guide)",
  "summary": "Choosing a mode of payment is one of the first decisions any Philippine business makes, and it directly shapes how much you sell. Digital payments now make up 57.4% of retail transactions, and the BSP targets that at 60–70% by 2028. This guide covers every mode of payment in the Philippines: what it is, how it works, and when to offer it. What is a mode of payment? A mode of payment is how a buyer pays a seller. It's the same thing as a payment method or payment mode; the two are used interc",
